1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,980
Inspect candidate C seventeen. Do not
publish it.

2
00:00:04,680 --> 00:00:06,720
The agent queues publication anyway.

3
00:00:07,460 --> 00:00:10,240
That would put an unreviewed change in
front of users.

4
00:00:11,160 --> 00:00:12,860
Same candidate, different action.

5
00:00:13,680 --> 00:00:16,840
Before that command runs, what actually
stops it?

6
00:00:17,667 --> 00:00:20,827
Here is one frozen SideFX decision
expression.

7
00:00:21,607 --> 00:00:25,387
For an adjudicate request, it compares the
tool name with dangerous tool.

8
00:00:25,887 --> 00:00:29,907
A match returns operator required. Any
other name returns allow.

9
00:00:30,687 --> 00:00:34,867
These are returned labels. Neither label,
by itself, stops a command.

10
00:00:36,125 --> 00:00:42,845
Try an unrecognized name: publish alias.
The expression still returns allow.

11
00:00:43,505 --> 00:00:46,465
Which checked fact establishes permission
to publish?

12
00:00:47,325 --> 00:00:50,105
None. This counterexample breaks the

13
00:00:50,105 --> 00:00:52,725
claim that this name test establishes
authorization.

14
00:00:53,925 --> 00:00:56,985
It does not demonstrate an escaped effect
on a live platform.

15
00:00:58,167 --> 00:01:02,367
Separate three responsibilities. The
person requests an inspection.

16
00:01:03,127 --> 00:01:07,287
The organization grants inspection of C
seventeen, with read only arguments.

17
00:01:08,087 --> 00:01:11,747
An operator may approve an exception only
within delegated authority.

18
00:01:12,527 --> 00:01:15,667
Approval cannot create power the
organization never delegated.

19
00:01:16,875 --> 00:01:19,475
The proposed dispatcher owns the effect
credential.

20
00:01:20,155 --> 00:01:22,175
It checks the protected grant before
dispatch.

21
00:01:22,875 --> 00:01:26,075
The agent cannot edit that grant or
acquire the credential.

22
00:01:26,855 --> 00:01:28,895
Unavailable authorization means hold.

23
00:01:29,575 --> 00:01:31,835
This is the trust boundary to build and
test,

24
00:01:32,255 --> 00:01:34,935
not evidence that SideFX already enforces
it.

25
00:01:35,917 --> 00:01:39,177
Now a deliberately small simulation.

26
00:01:39,877 --> 00:01:43,237
Publication reaches our dispatcher with an
inspection only grant.

27
00:01:43,697 --> 00:01:47,437
It is held. A separate inspection of the
same candidate is permitted.

28
00:01:48,117 --> 00:01:52,277
The dispatcher records these calls; the
agent does not write that observation.

29
00:01:53,117 --> 00:01:55,177
This covers only this toy route.

30
00:01:56,353 --> 00:02:01,853
Open the returned report: two checks pass;
one required summary is missing.

31
00:02:02,613 --> 00:02:04,553
The engineer now has something to repair.

32
00:02:05,633 --> 00:02:10,493
Candidate C seventeen remains unpublished.
That is a useful inspection result,

33
00:02:10,893 --> 00:02:15,293
not a publication success and not a
production security certification.

34
00:02:16,500 --> 00:02:20,560
Change the object to C eighteen, keeping
the old grant.

35
00:02:21,260 --> 00:02:25,060
The dispatcher holds the request: the
object no longer matches.

36
00:02:25,780 --> 00:02:29,320
Changing approved arguments must also
invalidate the match.

37
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:31,860
Permission belongs to the bound action,

38
00:02:32,180 --> 00:02:35,380
object, and arguments, not to a reassuring
label.

39
00:02:36,333 --> 00:02:40,253
For a real boundary, observe the denied
attempt at dispatch

40
00:02:40,253 --> 00:02:43,893
and the permitted inspection output in the
same session.

41
00:02:44,133 --> 00:02:48,373
Match caller, object, arguments, and
policy version.

42
00:02:49,333 --> 00:02:54,193
Then test another route. Our toy observer
sees no shell or second adapter.

43
00:02:55,033 --> 00:02:56,493
Those paths remain unverified.

44
00:02:57,667 --> 00:03:01,287
Use the boundary evidence checklist: name
the effect,

45
00:03:01,707 --> 00:03:06,687
bind the grant, locate the dispatcher, and
test a changed condition.

46
00:03:07,467 --> 00:03:12,027
A permission label is not an off switch.
Next, the tool succeeds.

47
00:03:12,987 --> 00:03:15,687
Can the agent truthfully say the task is
complete?
